# TalkFirst mobile — API base URL
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (or `.env`) next to `app.json` and restart
# Metro. Expo only reads variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ and inlines them
# into the JS bundle at build time, so a change requires a Metro restart — a
# Fast Refresh is not enough.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What you must set here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use your DEVELOPMENT MACHINE'S LAN IP, not localhost and not 10.0.2.2:
#
#   http://192.168.1.20:4000/api/v1    <- replace 192.168.1.20 with your IP
#
# The phone and the dev machine must be on the SAME network (same Wi-Fi / same
# LAN). A phone on mobile data, or on a guest Wi-Fi that isolates clients, can
# never reach the API and will fail with a timeout.
#
# Find your LAN IP:
#   Windows : ipconfig            -> "IPv4 Address" of the active adapter
#   macOS   : ipconfig getifaddr en0
#   Linux   : hostname -I         (first address)
# The API must also listen on 0.0.0.0 (not only 127.0.0.1) for the LAN IP to work.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-target values
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android emulator     : http://10.0.2.2:4000/api/v1
#                        (10.0.2.2 is the emulator's alias for the host machine.
#                         This is the ONLY environment where it resolves; it is
#                         also what the app falls back to, in dev, when this
#                         variable is unset.)
# iOS simulator        : http://localhost:4000/api/v1
#                        (the iOS simulator shares the host's network stack)
# Physical device      : http://<your-LAN-IP>:4000/api/v1   e.g. http://192.168.1.20:4000/api/v1
#                        (works for both Expo Go and a dev build)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Failure mode if this is wrong or missing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outside the Android emulator the app refuses to guess: with this variable
# unset it throws immediately, naming this variable, instead of failing later
# with an unexplained network error. See `src/lib/config.ts`.
#
# Uncomment and edit the line below.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:4000/api/v1
